## 12. Fallback endpoint variants (when props are NOT provided)

These fire only when `App.tsx` does not pass the corresponding callback — i.e., when the component is used standalone.

### 12.1 From `NotificationDropdown.tsx`

| Action | Method | Endpoint | Body |
|---|---|---|---|
| Accept invite | `PUT` | `/api/group-invites?id={inviteId}&group_id={groupId}` | `{ user_id, status: "accepted", group_id }` |
| Decline invite | `PUT` | `/api/group-invites?id={inviteId}&group_id={groupId}` | `{ id: inviteId, status: "declined", user_id, group_id }` |

### 12.2 From `NotificationsPage.tsx`

| Action | Method | Endpoint | Body |
|---|---|---|---|
| Accept invite | `POST` | `/api/groups/{groupId}/join` | `{ user_id, group_id }` |
| Decline invite | `PUT` | `/api/group-invites` | `{ id: inviteId, status: "rejected" }` |

