## 13. Notification object shape

Both components read these fields from each `Notification`:

```ts
{
  id: number;
  type: string;               // "like" | "react" | "comment" | "reply" | "follow" | "share" | "group_invite" | "invite" | "birthday" | "event" | "product" | ...
  actor_id: number;           // sender of the notification
  entity_id: number;          // the thing being acted on (post id, group id, etc.)
  entity_type?: string;       // "post" | "reel" | "story" | "song" | "product" | "event" | "group_post" | "group" | "profile"
  message: string;            // human-readable description
  is_read: 0 | 1;
  created_at: string;
  updated_at?: string;
  reaction_type?: string;     // for reactions — "like" | "love" | "haha" | "wow" | "sad" | "angry" | "fire" | ...
  actors_json?: string;       // JSON array of extra actor ids (for stacked avatars)
  actors_count?: number;
  group_id?: number;          // for group invites
  invite_id?: number;         // for group invites
  group_name?: string;
  preview_text?: string;      // snippet of the content (post text, comment text...)
  preview_image?: string;     // thumbnail of the content
  actor_name?: string;        // denormalized actor name
  actor_image?: string;       // denormalized actor avatar
  target_type?: string;       // alternative to entity_type
  target_id?: number;         // alternative to entity_id
}
```

