## 15. Notes on differences between the two components

| Feature | `NotificationDropdown.tsx` | `NotificationsPage.tsx` |
|---|---|---|
| Fetch notifications | ❌ never | ❌ never (parent only) |
| Mark all read | ✅ `onMarkAllRead` prop → `PATCH /api/notifications` | ✅ `onMarkAllAsRead` prop → `PATCH /api/notifications` |
| Mark single read | ❌ not exposed | ✅ optimistic local flip; real `POST /api/notifications/{id}/read` lives in `App.tsx` |
| Toggle read/unread | ❌ | ✅ local-only, **no API** |
| Delete | ❌ | ✅ via `onDeleteNotification` → `DELETE /api/notifications?id=` |
| Load more | ❌ | ✅ `onLoadMore` → `GET /api/notifications` |
| Accept invite fallback | `PUT /api/group-invites?id=&group_id=` with `status: "accepted"` | `POST /api/groups/{groupId}/join` |
| Decline invite fallback | `PUT /api/group-invites?id=&group_id=` with `status: "declined"` | `PUT /api/group-invites` with `status: "rejected"` |
| Sections (New / Today / Earlier) | ❌ flat list | ✅ sorted into 3 sections |
| Search | ❌ | ✅ client-side filter over `message`, `type`, `actor.name` |
| Simulated mode | ❌ | ✅ `simulateApi` prop delays operations by 500ms |

**Neither component performs a `GET` on its own.** The list arrives pre-populated via props, which is why the endpoints for fetch/delete/mark-all/load-more all live in **`App.tsx`** (`fetchNotifications`, `loadMoreNotifications`, `markAllNotificationsAsRead`, `deleteNotification`, `openNotificationTarget`).